    { "row": "R16", "editions": ["magnusim"], "ui_control": { "reach": "Run panel → Continue", "selector": "#modal-run-continue", "answers": ["#rcn-new", "#rcn-as-was"] }, "notes": "RH3: once the study's numerics differ from what the run started with (numerics_used), run_continue numerics \"new\" | \"as_was\" are the person's Continue question's answers \"Continue with the new numerics\" (#rcn-new) and \"Continue as it was\" (#rcn-as-was) in #modal-run-continue. Neither side chooses silently: the person's Continue asks first (Cancel posts nothing), the Assistant's run_continue with numerics \"\" is refused choose_numerics with no card, and the route refuses a Continue that does not say (409 choose_numerics, nothing queued). The question, the card and the refusals list the same differences (runReopen.ts numericsDiff). \"new\" goes on with the study's numerics and the run records them (an applied numerics entry in continue_changes, the Health block's earlier part names it); \"as_was\" with what it started with. assistant-parity-ui.spec.js checks the two answers with R35", "paths": [{ "tool": "compute", "where": { "action": "run_continue" }, "routes": ["run.continue"] }, { "tool": "compute", "where": { "action": "run_continue", "numerics": ["new", "as_was"] }, "routes": ["run.continue", "queue.add"] }] },
